Description: Let GNOME Shell hand a key pressed in a menu to the focused window.
 A stage grab receives all key events, so a shortcut of the focused window pressed while a GNOME Shell menu is open
 never reaches the window. For a global menu, whose items show the shortcuts of the window, the shortcut should act
 as if the menu were not open. meta_display_forward_key_event() delivers a key event, which a stage grab received,
 to the client with the keyboard focus, as it is delivered without a grab, once the stage is not grabbed anymore.
 GNOME Shell closes the menu, which ends the grab, and then forwards the key press. With
 meta_display_set_grab_keeps_keyboard_focus() of keep-keyboard-focus.patch, the window kept its keyboard focus
 during the grab and receives the modifier state when the grab ends, so the key reaches it with the modifiers held,
 and the release of the key follows without a grab.
 .
 The test /wayland/keep-keyboard-focus/forward-key of wayland-keep-keyboard-focus checks that Ctrl+N pressed during
 a grab is not forwarded while the stage is grabbed, and that the client receives N with Ctrl held once the grab
 ended, followed by the releases of N and Ctrl.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-25

